- pointermove document:
  - if pointer lock and state playing: yaw -= movementX*0.0021; pitch -= movementY*0.0019.
  - else if dragging pointer id matches: use movement dx from last.
- pointerup: end drag, if button 2 zoomHeld=false.
- But on touch, pointerdown on canvas when touch-ui buttons? Buttons are above canvas (z-index) and pointer-events auto, so canvas won't get event. Stick zone too. Good.
- `canvas.addEventListener('pointerdown'...)` request pointer lock on mouse click when playing. But if clicking to look while not locked and button 0, call requestPointerLock. Could conflict with drag fallback. Do requestPointerLock if no lock and state playing; also set dragging for fallback. If pointer lock succeeds, drag irrelevant.
- `document.addEventListener('pointerlockchange', ...)`: if desktop & state playing & pointerLockElement !== canvas → pauseGame(). But if request fails pointerlockerror no change. Good.
- `pointerlockerror`: do nothing.

Potential issue: user clicks Resume button; requestPointerLock inside resume click. Good.

Touch stick:
```js
const stickZone=$('stick-zone'), stickBase=$('stick-base'), stickKnob=$('stick-knob');
let stickId=null;
function setStickFromEvent(e) {
 const rect = stickBase.getBoundingClientRect();
 const cx=rect.left+rect.width/2, cy=rect.top+rect.height/2;
 let dx=e.clientX-cx, dy=e.clientY-cy;
 const max=rect.width*0.34;
 const len=Math.hypot(dx,dy);
 if (len>max) {dx*=max/len; dy*=max/len;}
 stickKnob.style.transform=`translate(${dx}px,${dy}px)`;
 stickX=dx/max; stickY=-dy/max; // up positive
}
stickZone pointerdown: if state playing, stickId=e.pointerId, setPointerCapture, class active, setStick...
pointermove if id...
pointerup/cancel: reset.
```
